(202171, 11381, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  i like the textured background, the lighting is pretty even (if not perfect), too.  i want to have the kind of view you have there!!!  being totally clueless at postprocessing (except for some of the basic steps), i really don''t know what to suggest, but the image doesn''t quite look real in the window.  the only other thing that you might want to consider (and probably already have) is that this is a very symmetrical photo and a square format would''ve enhanced that even further in my mind.  good work overall :)<br/></td>', 'challenge met.  i like the textured background, the lighting is pretty even (if not perfect), too.  i want to have the kind of view you have there!!!  being totally clueless at postprocessing (except for some of the basic steps), i really don''t know what to suggest, but the image doesn''t quite look real in the window.  the only other thing that you might want to consider (and probably already have) is that this is a very symmetrical photo and a square format would''ve enhanced that even further in my mind.  good work overall :)', '2003-01-28 12:01:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(202173, 11666, 327, '<td valign="top">great perspective view.</td>', 'great perspective view.', '2003-01-28 12:01:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(202174, 11523, 327, '<td valign="top">admire this shot, good work.</td>', 'admire this shot, good work.', '2003-01-28 12:01:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(202183, 11518, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  i like the tree reflecting in the windows a lot, i was looking around for a shot like that this week but didnt'' find anything.  a couple of things that i would''ve considered changing in your photo (and you probably have, and decided they didn''t work) is cropping out the foreground in front of the bushes.  i don''t think it adds to the picture.  a little more contrast would''ve made the photo "pop" more.  a difficult thing to control are lines, especially when shooting up a building.  they don''t look quite straight at the top.  centering yourself in front of the middle window (i think you were probably positioned a little to the left) might have reduced the uneven lines, and i would''ve also tried playing around with a little rotation, even if that makes the windows not quite level, just because the top of the photo is the most noticeable.  lastly, you seem to have vignetting on the edges of your photo.  is that from a filter maybe?  i have that problem, too, sometimes, and try and take pictures a little wider than i need and then crop the picture i actually want out of the center.  depending on what was around you that may of course not have been possible.  i do like the symmetry of your photo.  :)</td>', 'challenge met.  i like the tree reflecting in the windows a lot, i was looking around for a shot like that this week but didnt'' find anything.  a couple of things that i would''ve considered changing in your photo (and you probably have, and decided they didn''t work) is cropping out the foreground in front of the bushes.  i don''t think it adds to the picture.  a little more contrast would''ve made the photo "pop" more.  a difficult thing to control are lines, especially when shooting up a building.  they don''t look quite straight at the top.  centering yourself in front of the middle window (i think you were probably positioned a little to the left) might have reduced the uneven lines, and i would''ve also tried playing around with a little rotation, even if that makes the windows not quite level, just because the top of the photo is the most noticeable.  lastly, you seem to have vignetting on the edges of your photo.  is that from a filter maybe?  i have that problem, too, sometimes, and try and take pictures a little wider than i need and then crop the picture i actually want out of the center.  depending on what was around you that may of course not have been possible.  i do like the symmetry of your photo.  :)', '2003-01-28 12:08:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(202191, 11469, 573, '<td valign="top">Looks like something I might have seen in a model home.  Is that a Red Flier? <br/>The only thing in this photo that I feel could have made an improvement, since you could have used selection tools, is remove the distracting image behind the sheers and add something woodsy or country.</td>', 'Looks like something I might have seen in a model home.  Is that a Red Flier? The only thing in this photo that I feel could have made an improvement, since you could have used selection tools, is remove the distracting image behind the sheers and add something woodsy or country.', '2003-01-28 12:13:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(202211, 11559, 472, '<td valign="top">i do like the symmettry on this. i dont like that the pic seems a hair tilted to the right and that right edge is cut off unequally. and that the right edge is dark. I''m not sure how much the filter does for this pic. I think I might have rather seen it leveled and either in color or toned using the channel mixer.</td>', 'i do like the symmettry on this. i dont like that the pic seems a hair tilted to the right and that right edge is cut off unequally. and that the right edge is dark. I''m not sure how much the filter does for this pic. I think I might have rather seen it leveled and either in color or toned using the channel mixer.', '2003-01-28 12:23:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(202212, 11491, 573, '<td valign="top">Cool use of image manipulation, simple but dramatic.</td>', 'Cool use of image manipulation, simple but dramatic.', '2003-01-28 12:24:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(202223, 11518, 5044, '<td valign="top">I really like the reflections in the windows. Why is it so muddled. The reflection looks very caotic. Looks cool. The rest of the picture lacks something though.</td>', 'I really like the reflections in the windows. Why is it so muddled. The reflection looks very caotic. Looks cool. The rest of the picture lacks something though.', '2003-01-28 12:28:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(202234, 11402, 5044, '<td valign="top">Nice composition. Good sharp focus as well. I find the sky MUCH too blue though. The church looks like it is set against a "blue screen".</td>', 'Nice composition. Good sharp focus as well. I find the sky MUCH too blue though. The church looks like it is set against a "blue screen".', '2003-01-28 12:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(202237, 11362, 5044, '<td valign="top">Why isn''t the bell ringing? Nice job.</td>', 'Why isn''t the bell ringing? Nice job.', '2003-01-28 12:31:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(202239, 11625, 2011, '<td valign="top">Sorry, dont like the way you cut the top in PS.  A case of too much work on a perfectly good photo.5</td>', 'Sorry, dont like the way you cut the top in PS.  A case of too much work on a perfectly good photo.5', '2003-01-28 12:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(202242, 11624, 5044, '<td valign="top">Neat illusion.</td>', 'Neat illusion.', '2003-01-28 12:35:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(202246, 11642, 3585, '<td valign="top">Charming image, has the look and feel of the beginning of 20th century colorized postcards.</td>', 'Charming image, has the look and feel of the beginning of 20th century colorized postcards.', '2003-01-28 12:37:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(202252, 11489, 1078, '<td valign="top">I think this is a shot that would have benefitted from being perfectly in front of the window instead of just off to the side.  Don''t get me wrong -- I''m guessing you did so to try to avoid your reflection in the window which would have been still more distracting -- so other than some Photoshop work, maybe my suggestion is simply "impossible."  With all that great wood, I think I might also have backed off a little, left the window the dominant feature in the shot, put it more or less in one corner, and added in some more good texture that would have helped even more to give the window a setting.</td>', 'I think this is a shot that would have benefitted from being perfectly in front of the window instead of just off to the side.  Don''t get me wrong -- I''m guessing you did so to try to avoid your reflection in the window which would have been still more distracting -- so other than some Photoshop work, maybe my suggestion is simply "impossible."  With all that great wood, I think I might also have backed off a little, left the window the dominant feature in the shot, put it more or less in one corner, and added in some more good texture that would have helped even more to give the window a setting.', '2003-01-28 12:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(202256, 11537, 3585, '<td valign="top">Needs just a little something to liven up this scene: a leaning object, a shadow, a twig etc.</td>', 'Needs just a little something to liven up this scene: a leaning object, a shadow, a twig etc.', '2003-01-28 12:44:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(202262, 11498, 5044, '<td valign="top">Nice old fashioned styled picture. I''m not sure the border is quite acurate for the style. The birds in the sky add just the right element. Good job.</td>', 'Nice old fashioned styled picture. I''m not sure the border is quite acurate for the style. The birds in the sky add just the right element. Good job.', '2003-01-28 12:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(202266, 11458, 1078, '<td valign="top">I have a number of comments and I hope they don''t come across too harshly.  First, I''m not sure if the photo itself has that much interest to it.  Second, there are a number of filters that shouldn''t be used except in extreme cases and usually only with a lot of other work involved -- I think maybe the puzzle filter is one of them.  Finally, the selection around the puzzle piece is a little rough -- it may be that you need to spend a little more time learning how to use those selection tools.  Generally speaking, humans want to see light from the top down (something we''re conditioned to because of the sun) -- so while the drop shadow on the puzzle piece was a nice idea, you might want to switch it so that it''s on the opposite ("bottom") side of the piece -- which it looks like would help it match the lighting on the rest of the puzzle pieces.</td>', 'I have a number of comments and I hope they don''t come across too harshly.  First, I''m not sure if the photo itself has that much interest to it.  Second, there are a number of filters that shouldn''t be used except in extreme cases and usually only with a lot of other work involved -- I think maybe the puzzle filter is one of them.  Finally, the selection around the puzzle piece is a little rough -- it may be that you need to spend a little more time learning how to use those selection tools.  Generally speaking, humans want to see light from the top down (something we''re conditioned to because of the sun) -- so while the drop shadow on the puzzle piece was a nice idea, you might want to switch it so that it''s on the opposite ("bottom") side of the piece -- which it looks like would help it match the lighting on the rest of the puzzle pieces.', '2003-01-28 12:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(202268, 11433, 3585, '<td valign="top">Nice tones, solid composition and for once, a very effective border</td>', 'Nice tones, solid composition and for once, a very effective border', '2003-01-28 12:50:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(202270, 11660, 1078, '<td valign="top">The angles on this seem strange -- I''m guessing because you were trying to get those great clouds "perfectly" in the shot.  Nothing seems to perfectly line up with any of the shot''s edges (though that may be an optical illusion along the top and bottom).  But it''s the sides of the shot -- the slight angle on the left and the sharper angle on the right that disturb me -- as well as the way the window edges were cropped off on the right hand side but remain on the left.  Basically, the composition just feels unbalanced all around.</td>', 'The angles on this seem strange -- I''m guessing because you were trying to get those great clouds "perfectly" in the shot.  Nothing seems to perfectly line up with any of the shot''s edges (though that may be an optical illusion along the top and bottom).  But it''s the sides of the shot -- the slight angle on the left and the sharper angle on the right that disturb me -- as well as the way the window edges were cropped off on the right hand side but remain on the left.  Basically, the composition just feels unbalanced all around.', '2003-01-28 12:52:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(202274, 11610, 1078, '<td valign="top">I''m trying to determine if the "yellow" along the very top of the shot disturbs me or not -- I guess if I have to question it, it does somewhat.  I do like how it echoes the color of the stars at the top of the cuppola, but I think it might have been more effective to leave it off.  Which, admittedly would have thrown off the rest of the composition unless you moved a little more to the center and got a bit more roof along the top of the shot.  Otherwise, the right to left symmetry of the shot works well as does the verall exposure.</td>', 'I''m trying to determine if the "yellow" along the very top of the shot disturbs me or not -- I guess if I have to question it, it does somewhat.  I do like how it echoes the color of the stars at the top of the cuppola, but I think it might have been more effective to leave it off.  Which, admittedly would have thrown off the rest of the composition unless you moved a little more to the center and got a bit more roof along the top of the shot.  Otherwise, the right to left symmetry of the shot works well as does the verall exposure.', '2003-01-28 12:55:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(202275, 11662, 3599, '<td valign="top">I like the reflection of the sky in the windows.  I think I would have not included the blue in the upper right hand corner.  The focus seems a little bit too soft.  I would have liked to see more detail in the bricks.  Good work and good luck.</td>', 'I like the reflection of the sky in the windows.  I think I would have not included the blue in the upper right hand corner.  The focus seems a little bit too soft.  I would have liked to see more detail in the bricks.  Good work and good luck.', '2003-01-28 12:55:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(202280, 11537, 1078, '<td valign="top">I like the direction this shot is going and I think it has a lot of promise.  I think, perhaps, I would have tried to crop it slightly less tightly at the top of the shot -- match the margins at either side -- though this may not have been possible.  More importantly, their seems to be something strange going on with the straight lines in the shot.  The sides of the window seem to be straight up and down, but the bottoms of the window slope down to the right.  I think this is an image that needs to be square all the way around -- easy to fix in Photoshop with the transform tool.</td>', 'I like the direction this shot is going and I think it has a lot of promise.  I think, perhaps, I would have tried to crop it slightly less tightly at the top of the shot -- match the margins at either side -- though this may not have been possible.  More importantly, their seems to be something strange going on with the straight lines in the shot.  The sides of the window seem to be straight up and down, but the bottoms of the window slope down to the right.  I think this is an image that needs to be square all the way around -- easy to fix in Photoshop with the transform tool.', '2003-01-28 12:59:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(202282, 11498, 3585, '<td valign="top">lots of charm and good border</td>', 'lots of charm and good border', '2003-01-28 13:01:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(202285, 11458, 3599, '<td valign="top">This is a great idea and I wonder how well it will do.  I would have cropped some off of the top because the puzzle piece lines just stop which almost ruins the illusion.</td>', 'This is a great idea and I wonder how well it will do.  I would have cropped some off of the top because the puzzle piece lines just stop which almost ruins the illusion.', '2003-01-28 13:05:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(202286, 11536, 1078, '<td valign="top">Great contrast and love the sinuous lines of the shot.  It makes an excellent abstract.  There are nits, and I don''t know that you can do anything about them, but I''ll point them out anyway.  All of these beautiful clean lines are broken up by that wire (?) in the upper right corner -- go cut it down.  ;-)  There are also some strange shadows -- perhaps cast by the same wire, or by cousins orwho knows in the window section -- these are much less distracting than that wire.  There are some ways, not too hard to use, to get rid of all of those problems if you''d like some help.</td>', 'Great contrast and love the sinuous lines of the shot.  It makes an excellent abstract.  There are nits, and I don''t know that you can do anything about them, but I''ll point them out anyway.  All of these beautiful clean lines are broken up by that wire (?) in the upper right corner -- go cut it down.  ;-)  There are also some strange shadows -- perhaps cast by the same wire, or by cousins orwho knows in the window section -- these are much less distracting than that wire.  There are some ways, not too hard to use, to get rid of all of those problems if you''d like some help.', '2003-01-28 13:05:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(202290, 11464, 3599, '<td valign="top">Maybe more light on the other side of the door would have brought the colors out more.  Good job and good luck.</td>', 'Maybe more light on the other side of the door would have brought the colors out more.  Good job and good luck.', '2003-01-28 13:07:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(202293, 11537, 3599, '<td valign="top">Without the title I''m not sure I''d know this is an old house.  I think instead of focusing on the area below the window I would have tilted the camera up and get more of those cracks around the window.  There just isn''t enough detail in the wall below.  Good work and good luck.</td>', 'Without the title I''m not sure I''d know this is an old house.  I think instead of focusing on the area below the window I would have tilted the camera up and get more of those cracks around the window.  There just isn''t enough detail in the wall below.  Good work and good luck.', '2003-01-28 13:09:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(202294, 11511, 1078, '<td valign="top">I like it -- I think it could use some tweaks here and there -- but I like it.  The horizontal lines near the bottom of the shot seem to be perfectly horizontal, but they''re off just enough to notice as you look at them higher up the wall.  The red and blue seems to be just a touch dark or maybe flat -- it''s hard to adjust the whole photo to fix those without blowing out the snow, but since you were allowed unbounded Photoshop tweaks, that should be easy to overcome (as with the fixing the lines to horizontal).  Love the symmetry, and the half windows at the top.</td>', 'I like it -- I think it could use some tweaks here and there -- but I like it.  The horizontal lines near the bottom of the shot seem to be perfectly horizontal, but they''re off just enough to notice as you look at them higher up the wall.  The red and blue seems to be just a touch dark or maybe flat -- it''s hard to adjust the whole photo to fix those without blowing out the snow, but since you were allowed unbounded Photoshop tweaks, that should be easy to overcome (as with the fixing the lines to horizontal).  Love the symmetry, and the half windows at the top.', '2003-01-28 13:11:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(202295, 11379, 3599, '<td valign="top">The texture, colors, contrast, and framing make this a nice photo.  Making this sharper would make it a great photo.  Good work and good luck.</td>', 'The texture, colors, contrast, and framing make this a nice photo.  Making this sharper would make it a great photo.  Good work and good luck.', '2003-01-28 13:12:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(202296, 11426, 3585, '<td valign="top">If you could have created some eye contact between the two the illusion would be much more powerfull, good work.</td>', 'If you could have created some eye contact between the two the illusion would be much more powerfull, good work.', '2003-01-28 13:14:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(202297, 11498, 3599, '<td valign="top">The building looks like it is falling away from me.  I don''t know hoe to avoid this phenomenon.  I didn''t like the grain but when I saw the border I changed my mind because I think it fits with the "old" look.  Other then the leaning look I like this photo a lot.</td>', 'The building looks like it is falling away from me.  I don''t know hoe to avoid this phenomenon.  I didn''t like the grain but when I saw the border I changed my mind because I think it fits with the "old" look.  Other then the leaning look I like this photo a lot.', '2003-01-28 13:15:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(202298, 11609, 3599, '<td valign="top">The red stands out brilliantly.  I like the tree in the foreground.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'The red stands out brilliantly.  I like the tree in the foreground.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2003-01-28 13:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(202299, 11357, 2130, '<td valign="top">original :)</td>', 'original :)', '2003-01-28 13:17:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(202301, 11498, 2130, '<td valign="top">I like the birds and the sky...it´s all so spookie...definently a 10</td>', 'I like the birds and the sky...it´s all so spookie...definently a 10', '2003-01-28 13:19:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(202308, 11426, 2130, '<td valign="top">very, very good</td>', 'very, very good', '2003-01-28 13:27:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(202309, 11594, 2130, '<td valign="top">so natural and happy, I love this one</td>', 'so natural and happy, I love this one', '2003-01-28 13:28:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(202349, 11580, 472, '<td valign="top">excellent. i wonder how this would have looked un altered? the lighting is great, looks like a video game.</td>', 'excellent. i wonder how this would have looked un altered? the lighting is great, looks like a video game.', '2003-01-28 13:53:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(202350, 11661, 472, '<td valign="top">excellent graphic elements!</td>', 'excellent graphic elements!', '2003-01-28 13:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(202352, 11524, 472, '<td valign="top">oh wow! this is incredible .. very evocative.  if the symettry was a little more perfect it would really kick butt</td>', 'oh wow! this is incredible .. very evocative.  if the symettry was a little more perfect it would really kick butt', '2003-01-28 13:54:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(202356, 11469, 472, '<td valign="top">a well taken shot but not a very interesting subject.  go in search of interesting windows or doors! :)</td>', 'a well taken shot but not a very interesting subject.  go in search of interesting windows or doors! :)', '2003-01-28 13:56:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(202359, 11639, 472, '<td valign="top">would be better if the light was ON the window.  could have come back a different time of day?</td>', 'would be better if the light was ON the window.  could have come back a different time of day?', '2003-01-28 13:57:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(202361, 11662, 472, '<td valign="top">could be great but there is a focus issue.</td>', 'could be great but there is a focus issue.', '2003-01-28 13:58:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(202363, 11364, 472, '<td valign="top">very very crisp shot with good lighting</td>', 'very very crisp shot with good lighting', '2003-01-28 13:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(202415, 11636, 811, '<td valign="top">My only suggestion would have been to crop some of the roof and sky out and show more of the shubbery.  Also, I think a different perspective (other than directly on) would have made it more dramatic.  Very interesting shot, and meets the challenge well!</td>', 'My only suggestion would have been to crop some of the roof and sky out and show more of the shubbery.  Also, I think a different perspective (other than directly on) would have made it more dramatic.  Very interesting shot, and meets the challenge well!', '2003-01-28 16:01:08.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(202422, 11504, 811, '<td valign="top">That''s a cool shot.  I think I understand why you left the top window in, but I think I would have liked it as well, or better, with it cropped out.  Love the silhouette.</td>', 'That''s a cool shot.  I think I understand why you left the top window in, but I think I would have liked it as well, or better, with it cropped out.  Love the silhouette.', '2003-01-28 16:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(202423, 11651, 4536, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. Nothing to critique, perfect as is.</td>', 'Beautiful. Nothing to critique, perfect as is.', '2003-01-28 16:14:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(202424, 11509, 4536, '<td valign="top">A reflection? Can''t wait for the tutorial on this one :). AWESOME!</td>', 'A reflection? Can''t wait for the tutorial on this one :). AWESOME!', '2003-01-28 16:17:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(202439, 11458, 5044, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot. How was this done? Is it a picture of a puzzle, or is this some kind of PS effect.</td>', 'I really like this shot. How was this done? Is it a picture of a puzzle, or is this some kind of PS effect.', '2003-01-28 16:40:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(202440, 11471, 714, '<td valign="top">Cool shot.  I love the curls.  The colors and lighting are excillent.</td>', 'Cool shot.  I love the curls.  The colors and lighting are excillent.', '2003-01-28 16:41:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(202442, 11512, 714, '<td valign="top">This just doesnt seem like it is in focus.  The background is to distracting. Did you try shooting the inside of the door?</td>', 'This just doesnt seem like it is in focus.  The background is to distracting. Did you try shooting the inside of the door?', '2003-01-28 16:42:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(202443, 11468, 714, '<td valign="top">I like the angle of the window.  color is good.  Sure seems like a dream.</td>', 'I like the angle of the window.  color is good.  Sure seems like a dream.', '2003-01-28 16:44:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(202444, 11618, 714, '<td valign="top">Different looking.   I like the effect you used.</td>', 'Different looking.   I like the effect you used.', '2003-01-28 16:45:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(202445, 11426, 714, '<td valign="top">So which one is the evil twin?  hehe.  Nice shot.  Great cropping work.  Good luck.</td>', 'So which one is the evil twin?  hehe.  Nice shot.  Great cropping work.  Good luck.', '2003-01-28 16:46:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(202446, 11364, 714, '<td valign="top">Now that is a macro of an eye.  Very nice.  looks good in b/w.</td>', 'Now that is a macro of an eye.  Very nice.  looks good in b/w.', '2003-01-28 16:47:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(202447, 11651, 714, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo.  I love the window and the colors. You chose a great angle.</td>', 'Excellent photo.  I love the window and the colors. You chose a great angle.', '2003-01-28 16:48:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(202448, 11513, 714, '<td valign="top">Simply, Yes.  Very interesting shot.  I like the distorted tree.</td>', 'Simply, Yes.  Very interesting shot.  I like the distorted tree.', '2003-01-28 16:50:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(202451, 11586, 714, '<td valign="top">The lighting is a bit bright,. maybe if you waited till early evening.</td>', 'The lighting is a bit bright,. maybe if you waited till early evening.', '2003-01-28 16:51:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(202454, 11491, 714, '<td valign="top">Very interesting effect.  I like the different shades of the shutters.  The colors are great.  Nice framing.</td>', 'Very interesting effect.  I like the different shades of the shutters.  The colors are great.  Nice framing.', '2003-01-28 16:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(202457, 11498, 255, '<td valign="top">i really like this--the graininess of the sky and the stark angles of the building work nicely together---and the birds frame the picture perfectly. great work!</td>', 'i really like this--the graininess of the sky and the stark angles of the building work nicely together---and the birds frame the picture perfectly. great work!', '2003-01-28 16:59:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(202462, 11612, 255, '<td valign="top">whoa--trippy--like two little ghosties! maybe i warped myself on stephen king, but this is pretty scary! ;)<br/>i really like the monotone coloring and the rain coming down---adds to the spookiness! nice work!</td>', 'whoa--trippy--like two little ghosties! maybe i warped myself on stephen king, but this is pretty scary! ;)i really like the monotone coloring and the rain coming down---adds to the spookiness! nice work!', '2003-01-28 17:06:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(202466, 11453, 255, '<td valign="top">very pretty coloring--you couldnt have asked for a better sky! the only thing i might have done differently was either cropped closer in to the center cloumns or wider to allow a little more room for the curves to be accented by the lines on either side. nice work!</td>', 'very pretty coloring--you couldnt have asked for a better sky! the only thing i might have done differently was either cropped closer in to the center cloumns or wider to allow a little more room for the curves to be accented by the lines on either side. nice work!', '2003-01-28 17:10:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(202468, 11513, 255, '<td valign="top">wow, the tree is very eye catching! good contrast between light and dark, solid and pattern.</td>', 'wow, the tree is very eye catching! good contrast between light and dark, solid and pattern.', '2003-01-28 17:11:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(202472, 11505, 255, '<td valign="top">this is great! the lines and curves work wonderfully together, and the window colors are very nicely accented by the yellowish walls.  great eye!</td>', 'this is great! the lines and curves work wonderfully together, and the window colors are very nicely accented by the yellowish walls.  great eye!', '2003-01-28 17:15:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(202474, 11468, 255, '<td valign="top">very cool. i love the angle of the window and the sporadic placement of the bricks around the frame---really enhances the dreaminess of the photo. and of course the face is very well done--gives the whole thing a sort of parallel universe alice in wonderland feel---maybe allen in wonderland? hehehhe! awesome work.</td>', 'very cool. i love the angle of the window and the sporadic placement of the bricks around the frame---really enhances the dreaminess of the photo. and of course the face is very well done--gives the whole thing a sort of parallel universe alice in wonderland feel---maybe allen in wonderland? hehehhe! awesome work.', '2003-01-28 17:20:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(202481, 11458, 255, '<td valign="top">sweet!!!!!! the photograph would be cool even with out the puzzle--i really like the contrast of the red door with the surrounding neutral colors. but of course i have to know how you did the puzzle! very creative! 10</td>', 'sweet!!!!!! the photograph would be cool even with out the puzzle--i really like the contrast of the red door with the surrounding neutral colors. but of course i have to know how you did the puzzle! very creative! 10', '2003-01-28 17:33:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(202490, 11635, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice sillhouettes, but not much else.   The crop adds a little interest, but not enough.  5 Swash</td>', 'Nice sillhouettes, but not much else.   The crop adds a little interest, but not enough.  5 Swash', '2003-01-28 18:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(202493, 11445, 1005, '<td valign="top">Solidly taken photo.  Focus is good, needs more contrast to work in black and white (to me at least).  While I KNOW there''s a door there due to the handle, it''s not enough, I need more to say this is a door subject photo.  6 Swash</td>', 'Solidly taken photo.  Focus is good, needs more contrast to work in black and white (to me at least).  While I KNOW there''s a door there due to the handle, it''s not enough, I need more to say this is a door subject photo.  6 Swash', '2003-01-28 18:10:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(202496, 11504, 2125, '<td valign="top">excellent!</td>', 'excellent!', '2003-01-28 18:19:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(202497, 11362, 2125, '<td valign="top">wow that is really cool!!</td>', 'wow that is really cool!!', '2003-01-28 18:19:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(202500, 11469, 2125, '<td valign="top">wow excellent only voted on a few but this is my fav...10</td>', 'wow excellent only voted on a few but this is my fav...10', '2003-01-28 18:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(202502, 11610, 2716, '<td valign="top">Neat.  Looks like a big funky eye.  I love it.  Looks like Gordon''s shot for archicecture.  Good job.  9</td>', 'Neat.  Looks like a big funky eye.  I love it.  Looks like Gordon''s shot for archicecture.  Good job.  9', '2003-01-28 18:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
