(204820, 11426, 5475, '<td valign="top">I had some great ideas for this challenge using Photoshop, but didn''t have time to work on them.  I''m happy to see someone took the relaxed rules to the limit!  This image is a lot of fun.  The image on the floor has lots of appeal...  the guy''s posture and look on his face work well.  The ''surprise'' on the main image is good. I feel the area in the background of the main image is a little cluttered.  Overall, lots of fun, thanks for using your creativity and giving us something unusual to look at this week!  9<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'I had some great ideas for this challenge using Photoshop, but didn''t have time to work on them.  I''m happy to see someone took the relaxed rules to the limit!  This image is a lot of fun.  The image on the floor has lots of appeal...  the guy''s posture and look on his face work well.  The ''surprise'' on the main image is good. I feel the area in the background of the main image is a little cluttered.  Overall, lots of fun, thanks for using your creativity and giving us something unusual to look at this week!  9JD Anderson', '2003-02-01 23:44:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(204823, 11509, 5475, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorites this week. I''m glad to see you took advantage of the relaxed editing rules this week.  Your manipulation is obvious, but it is not ''cheesy'' and it works very well.  I like the strong diagonals in the frame and the columns at the lower right are great.  Is this in DC?  As long as you were ''Photoshopping'' I would have cloned out the dark gray shadow at the top center of the frame.   I like this a lot and give it a 10! <br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'This is one of my favorites this week. I''m glad to see you took advantage of the relaxed editing rules this week.  Your manipulation is obvious, but it is not ''cheesy'' and it works very well.  I like the strong diagonals in the frame and the columns at the lower right are great.  Is this in DC?  As long as you were ''Photoshopping'' I would have cloned out the dark gray shadow at the top center of the frame.   I like this a lot and give it a 10! JD Anderson', '2003-02-01 23:47:27.000000', NULL, 1),
