(446714, 11433, 6999, '<td valign="top">Bllody hell Ben, I''ve just come across this on a trawl through the site (actually by way of JJ''s favourites): thought I''d seen all the really great photographs on this site, but his selections are almost as much a revelation as his photos. <br/> <br/>Wonderful stuff: the cleanness of those lines, the half-hidden window that makes me want to move into the shot to see what''s hidden. Almost worthy of Kertesz, in the sense of finding the extraordinary in the absolutely everyday.<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'Bllody hell Ben, I''ve just come across this on a trawl through the site (actually by way of JJ''s favourites): thought I''d seen all the really great photographs on this site, but his selections are almost as much a revelation as his photos.  Wonderful stuff: the cleanness of those lines, the half-hidden window that makes me want to move into the shot to see what''s hidden. Almost worthy of Kertesz, in the sense of finding the extraordinary in the absolutely everyday. Ed', '2003-10-10 21:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
